WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.200
There is a Congressman named Greg Meeks who
recently announced that he's supporting Michael

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.910
Bloomberg in the democratic primary.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:12.760
Now, Gregory Meeks is a Democrat and he is
black and Bloomberg has been having some issues

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.910
lately with comments about stop and frisk
and black Americans.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.760
And so these endorsements from minority members
of Congress are really important to Michael

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.919
Bloomberg being able to continue crafting
a narrative that is something other than the

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:32.550
vile racist, uh, which has been the characterization
of Bloomberg over the last couple of weeks.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.810
Well, Greg Meeks is helping to craft that
narrative.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:42.940
He showed up on CNN, he pulled the tired old,
but Bernie isn't a Democrat talking point,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.920
which is a lame talking point to start with
because it's not about issues.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.960
It's just a party membership argument.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:55.910
It's a form of exclusive tribalism, but it's
extra hilarious because Bloomberg just changed

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.290
from being a Republican to being a Democrat.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.370
So there's a ton to talk about here.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.060
Let's first watch the clip.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.519
Notice that Greg Meeks doesn't talk about
any policy here.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:10.600
It doesn't talk about who's better on healthcare,
who's better on economics, nothing.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.530
It's just Bernie isn't really a Democrat.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.689
Take a look.

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:19.240
The difference for me is Bernie Sanders is
not a Democrat.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.229
So I don't understand why Bernie Sanders,
who does not want to become a member of the

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:25.270
democratic party, he would run.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:30.420
And if he wins rule, you know, why does a
Democrat run as a Democrat?

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.820
We've asked him on a continuous basis, if
in fact you want to be the democratic nominee,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.479
you should be a Democrat.

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:39.499
If you're not a Democrat, you should not run.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.240
He should run as an independent.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.899
Uh, he's not a Democrat.

00:01:42.899 --> 00:01:48.369
So to me, I wouldn't allow a Republican to
run as a Democrat or for the democratic governor

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:49.369
run in the democratic.

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:50.580
I don't think he should be a Democrat.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:56.040
I think that he should say if he wants to
be a Democrat, he should register in the democratic

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.040
party.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.289
And then you can talk about running and to
be my representative, I want a Democrat to

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:06.280
be my representative, uh, as president of
the United States would be my nominee.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.230
And he raised a whole lot of money.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.230
You'll see what happens.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.230
Thank you very much.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.230
God.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.230
Pleasure.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.230
Okay.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.230
So first of all, debate the issues.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:20.209
If you support Bloomberg and not Bernie, argue
why Bloomberg is better than Bernie on the

00:02:20.209 --> 00:02:27.420
issues, what's their position on healthcare,
on education, on inequality, on for like whatever.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.840
Just pick a topic and argue why the person
you're supporting is better than Bernie, if

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.860
that's what you want to argue.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:34.860
Repeating.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.790
What was it four times there in a minute that
Bernie isn't a Democrat is not an argument.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:45.379
I don't care about tribalism and party, but
then it's layered too, which is if you want

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:47.230
to play the party game.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:53.270
Bloomberg was a Democrat until 2001 then became
a Republican to run for mayor, then became

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:59.500
an independent in 2007 to continue this sort
of persona of the independent thinker and

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.650
then became a Democrat in 2018 just a year
and a half ago, a presumably as a pretext

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:08.410
for what he is now doing, running for the
democratic presidential nomination.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:14.019
So it's all BS and the reality is meek says,
well, Bernie should just switch to being a

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:15.019
Democrat.

00:03:15.019 --> 00:03:19.270
Uh, now if, if, uh, he was running in the
democratic primary, if Bernie did that, they

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.110
would say Bernie's pandering.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:25.950
If Bernie Sanders took this guy's advice,
said, I am going to become a Democrat.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.689
If he did it, then Greg Meeks would be saying,
this is pandering.

00:03:29.689 --> 00:03:34.250
I don't, I want a real Democrat, not a guy
who switches his nomination.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:39.900
Uh, his party registration just to run for
president, which is exactly what the guy he's

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.970
supporting did Michael Bloomberg.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.489
So it's can't win for Bernie on this.

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:49.540
Greg Meeks would be the first to say Bernie
is only switching to pander.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.189
But then because Bernie did not switch party
registration, meek says, well, he's not really

00:03:53.189 --> 00:03:54.189
a Democrat.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:55.569
I want to vote for a Democrat.

00:03:55.569 --> 00:04:00.099
But then the most important thing again is
that none of this has to do with who's going

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:02.859
to be better for you on wages.

00:04:02.859 --> 00:04:04.719
Who's going to be better for you on healthcare?

00:04:04.719 --> 00:04:09.090
If for Republican ran with the right policies
against Trump, I'd support the Republican.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:14.400
Now, in reality, no one with those socially
democratic policies that I support would be

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.370
a Republican in 2020 United States.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.870
But it's besides the point, I don't care about
party registration.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:23.169
Note also that Bernie is in the democratic
leadership in the Senate.

00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:30.060
He's not just some outsider who has no integration
with the democratic party, so it's a circular

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.789
firing squad argument.

00:04:31.789 --> 00:04:33.919
It will never get anywhere.

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:39.740
Anyone who makes this argument already shows
they don't really care about reason and rationality.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:43.090
And then the problem is anyone who tries to
argue with somebody like Greg Meeks about

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.180
this is also going to fail because it's an
unwinnable argument no matter what.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:54.580
They will say why Bernie is wrong in this
particular case, and then zoom out as of December,

00:04:54.580 --> 00:05:01.230
2019 Gallup says only 28% of Americans are
registered Democrats.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:06.860
So what exactly are you trying to do by saying
if you aren't part of the club, we don't want

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:14.229
you when 72% of the country isn't part of
that club and is not a demo or aren't registered

00:05:14.229 --> 00:05:19.960
democratic voters, it's pointless tribalism
and it doesn't actually deal with the issues,

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.830
which is what I care about.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:23.240
Tell me what you think about this.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.690
Bernie's really a Democrat

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:29.590
meme that is continuing to sort of spread
like a virus in some circles.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:42.720
Let me know

00:05:42.720 --> 00:06:45.080
on Twitter.

